		<unit label="title" identifier="24.2" level="1">Elections</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="5" level="2">Candidates for Office</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="4" level="3">Conduct of Primaries</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>24.2-530</section_number>
	<catch_line>Who may vote in primary</catch_line>
	<text>
		All persons qualified to vote, pursuant to §§ 24.2-400 through 24.2-403, may vote at the primary. No person shall vote for the candidates of more than one party.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 24-367; 1970, c. 462, § 24.1-182; 1971, Ex. Sess., c. 205; 1976, c. 616; 1993, c. 641.</history>
</law>
